[
 {
  "id": "F1",
  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "line": 377,
  "title": "Landing publishes before its outer transaction commits, and never drains the feed",
  "detail": "`landed()` wraps `finish()` and the merge resolvers in a raw `this.store.db.transaction(...)`. That leaves `store.pendingPublications` unset. Each `resolveMergedRun` \u2192 `updateRun`/`resolveRun` then opens its own `chatTransaction`, which publishes its run messages as soon as its savepoint returns, while the outer landing transaction is still open (src/db/store.ts, around lines 668-681). Subscribers can therefore see merge and resolution messages that a later failure in the same transaction rolls back. Then `publishFeed()` returns early because `db.inTransaction` is true (around line 686), and nothing drains the feed after the outer commit. So the new `run.merged`, `land.landed` and resolution items wake SSE and long-poll consumers only when some unrelated publication happens. Fix: run the whole landing through one publication-buffered store transaction, for example a store method that reuses `chatTransaction`'s buffering for an outer block. Publish the buffered messages and drain the feed only after the outermost commit. Add a test that subscribes to the store and asserts no run or feed message is delivered before the landing commits, and that the landing's feed items are published right after it."
 },
 {
  "id": "F2",
  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "line": 378,
  "title": "A cancelled entry drops an already confirmed merge",
  "detail": "When the entry is no longer active, `landed()` returns before recording anything. That skips the entry transition, as intended, but it also skips every run merge record. A late observation can confirm the merge after a cancel: `awaitCi()` returns a `MERGED` observation (around line 458) and `landed()` discards it. Cancelled entries are not processed again on restart (around line 145), so the runs stay unmerged until the notifier happens to observe the merge with a valid `mergedAt`. Fix: keep the entry `cancelled`, but always record a merge GitHub confirmed for the PR's runs, through the same resolver path. Add a test: cancel the entry, then let the observation report MERGED. The entry stays cancelled and the runs are resolved as merged, with no second merge command."
 },
 {
  "id": "F3",
  "file": "src/land/queue.ts",
  "line": 375,
  "title": "Landing through the owner run still supersedes the PR's own rounds",
  "detail": "The round-1 fix covers an entry that names a round run: `ids` then holds the round and its owner. When the entry names the owner run, which test/land-queue.test.ts around line 1629 supports, `ids` is just the owner. Marking it merged then resolves a same-issue `needs_human` round of the same PR as `superseded`, not merged (src/db/store.ts `supersedeByIssue`, around 1785 and 1889). Reconciliation passes no exclusions either (src/integrations/github-notifier.ts around 204), so restart recovery can do the same. Main already does this, but the round-1 finding asked that the runs being landed be excluded from supersession, and a PR's rounds are among them. Fix: resolve every run that shares the landed PR (the owner and all its rounds) as merged, and exclude them from supersession, whichever run the entry names. Use one helper in both `landed()` and `reconcileMergedRuns`. Add a test that lands through the owner while a same-issue `needs_human` round exists, and that fails today."
 }
